This repository holds two kinds of work, and only one of them is mine to
license. See "Rights and preservation" in README.md.

1. THE ORIGINAL GAME

   "The Secret of Arendarvon Castle" (Addison-Wesley, 1985) by Hal Renko &
   Sam Edwards with Arend Rensink: its logic, text, world data, puzzles, and the
   ALADIN virtual machine and bytecode, in whatever form they appear here.

   Copyright rests with the authors or their publisher's successor.

2. MY CONTRIBUTIONS

   The structure, naming and commentary of the refactored source; the test
   harness, including the 6502 emulator and the re-implemented BBC BASIC host;
   the two front ends; the documentation and the map.

